{#
  Prose chrome for Markdown pages.

  base.njk emits `content` straight into `<main>`, which is right for the hand-built `.njk`
  pages: they carry full-bleed section backgrounds and supply their own containers. A Markdown
  page has neither, so it rendered edge-to-edge with no measure and no vertical rhythm — the
  stylesheet has no element-level rules for `p`, `ul` or `li`, only the `.prose-ki` component.

  Thirteen prompting pages used to paste this wrapper into their own body. Holding it in a layout
  means a guidance page added tomorrow is styled because it is a guidance page, not because
  someone remembered.

  The provenance footer is included here for the same reason, and for one more: thirty-five pages
  each ended with the include in their own Markdown body, which put a table of links to other
  repositories through the Markdown renderer as the page's closing section (KI-WEBSITE-SITE-024).
#}
<section class="section-parchment section-pad">
  <div class="page-container" style="max-width: 64rem;">
    <article class="prose-ki" style="max-width: none;">
      {% include "partials/up-link.njk" %}
      {{ content | safe }}
      {% include "partials/section-contents.njk" %}
      {% include "partials/sources.njk" %}
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
